{"id": "14fd136c-3a50-4d3e-985a-66a663749f2e", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check how your Bedrock invocations in us-east-1 identify their models over the last 14 days. That means finding where invocation data is recorded, such as model invocation logging or CloudTrail, and separating direct foundation-model IDs from inference profile IDs.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_GnUJDgKtkgHS0THl8WUfXg", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-model-id-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["searching-logs", "investigating-infrastructure-changes", "exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether any Amazon Bedrock runtime calls (InvokeModel, InvokeModelWithResponseStream, Converse, ConverseStream) in us-east-1 used a direct foundation-model ID (e.g. anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022-v2:0, or a foundation-model ARN) where an inference profile (system-defined like us.anthropic.... / global.anthropic..., or application inference profile ARN) should be used instead.",
  "context": "User asks: 'Are any of our Bedrock calls in us-east-1 using a direct model ID where we should be using an inference profile? Check the last 14 days.' This is a bounded audit, not a root-cause hunt. Bedrock runtime calls are data events and may NOT be in CloudTrail by default, so first discover what evidence exists: (1) Bedrock model invocation logging configuration (get_model_invocation_logging_configuration) and its CloudWatch Logs group / S3 bucket; query the modelId field in those logs; (2) CloudTrail (data event selectors on AWS::Bedrock::* or management events if available) for the caller identity, userAgent and requestParameters modelId; (3) CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics by ModelId dimension (note that inference profile usage shows the profile ID as ModelId) to see which model IDs are invoked. Also list the available inference profiles in us-east-1 (bedrock list_inference_profiles) and note which models REQUIRE an inference profile for on-demand throughput (invoking those directly would fail with a ValidationException/throughput error - look for such errors too). Also check which Bedrock foundation models are in use and whether they support on-demand direct invocation versus requiring a profile.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 123456789012", "region us-east-1", "Bedrock runtime", "Bedrock model invocation logging log group/bucket", "CloudWatch namespace AWS/Bedrock"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-09T21:20:00Z/2026-11-23T21:20:00Z",
  "criteria": "Report: (a) what data sources were available and what coverage gaps exist (e.g. invocation logging not enabled, no Bedrock data events in CloudTrail), (b) a list of distinct modelIds observed, classified as direct foundation model ID vs inference profile (system or application), with call counts and the calling principals/roles/applications where visible, (c) which direct-ID calls are ones that should move to an inference profile (e.g. models that require profiles, or where cross-region profile would improve throughput/resilience) and which are fine as direct, (d) any throughput/validation errors related to model ID usage. Be explicit if you cannot determine the answer, rather than guessing. Keep the report concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Bedrock model ID usage in us-east-1 over 14 days"}], "created_at": null}

